# workflows.allow -- the paths published to 9atatimer/workflows.
#
# One path or glob per line, relative to the repository root. `#` starts a
# comment. No negation. A path that no line names is not published, and a
# line that matches no file at the released commit refuses the whole
# publication. Runbook: docs/ops/tds-public.md.
#
# Publish the minimum the callers need: the three reusable workflows and
# exactly the files they fetch and run, nothing the engine's own tests,
# evals or fixtures hold.

# The three reusable workflows.
.github/workflows/ocr-review.yml
.github/workflows/review-settled.yml
.github/workflows/adherence.yml

# ocr-review.yml: sparse-checks out bin/ocr-review and lib/ocr-review.
bin/ocr-review
lib/ocr-review/**

# review-settled.yml: sparse-checks out these two files.
bin/review-settled
lib/review-settled.mjs

# adherence.yml: sparse-checks out bin/adhere, bin/decide, lib/decide and
# adherence; then `uv sync --frozen --no-dev` (pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
# .python-version, src/) and `npm ci` (node/package.json and lock).
# bin/decide and lib/decide are also fetched by template-tools'
# naatm-ci-magic.
bin/adhere
bin/decide
lib/decide/**
adherence/pyproject.toml
adherence/uv.lock
adherence/.python-version
adherence/src/**
adherence/node/package.json
adherence/node/package-lock.json
